--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1 +1,33 @@
-# Holiday_Project
\ No newline at end of file
+# Orlando Trip 2026
+
+Offline companion app for the school trip: itinerary, tip calculator, currency converter,
+packing list, spending tracker and an in-flight arcade. Built with React, Vite and Tailwind,
+and installable on your phone as a PWA.
+
+## Run it
+
+```bash
+npm install
+npm run dev      # http://localhost:5173
+npm run build    # production build into dist/
+npm run preview  # test the production build locally
+```
+
+## Put it on your phone (GitHub Pages, free, no limits)
+
+Phones only let you install an app from a secure (https) site. GitHub Pages gives you that for free:
+
+1. Push this repo to GitHub (branch `main`).
+2. On GitHub: **Settings -> Pages -> Build and deployment -> Source: GitHub Actions**.
+3. Wait about a minute for the **Deploy to GitHub Pages** run (Actions tab) to go green.
+4. Open `https://rishn12.github.io/Holiday_Project/` on your phone.
+5. **Android (Chrome):** menu (3 dots) -> *Install app*.
+   **iPhone (Safari):** Share button -> *Add to Home Screen*.
+6. Open the app once with Wi-Fi so it caches everything. After that it works offline.
+
+Every push to `main` redeploys automatically and the installed app updates itself.
+
+## Icons
+
+Icons live in `public/` (`pwa-192x192.png`, `pwa-512x512.png`, `pwa-maskable-512x512.png`,
+`apple-touch-icon.png`). They must be real PNGs at those exact sizes.
